<header><p class="st-kicker">duchy · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Duchy of Bavaria-Landshut</h1><p class="st-meta">1392 CE – 1503 CE · capital Landshut</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The richest of the late medieval Bavarian duchies, ruled from Landshut by the 'Rich Dukes' and famed for the Landshut Wedding of 1475.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1392 the three sons of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stephen-ii-duke-of-bavaria">Duke Stephen II</a> divided <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a>: Frederick took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria-landshut">Bavaria-Landshut</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-ii-duke-of-bavaria">John II</a> the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-bavaria-munich">Duchy of Bavaria-Munich</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stephen-iii-duke-of-bavaria">Stephen III</a> the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-bavaria-ingolstadt">Duchy of Bavaria-Ingolstadt</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/landshut">Landshut</a>, seat of the Lower Bavarian dukes since the 13th century, became capital of the wealthiest share, which gained part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-bavaria-straubing">Duchy of Bavaria-Straubing</a> in 1429 and all of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ingolstadt">Ingolstadt</a> in 1447.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Three successive dukes, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-xvi-duke-of-bavaria">Henry XVI</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-ix-duke-of-bavaria">Louis IX</a> and George, were known as the Rich for the treasure they amassed from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a>, salt tolls and strict financial administration, kept in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trausnitz-castle">Trausnitz</a> castle and the fortress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burghausen">Burghausen</a>. Louis IX founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/university-of-ingolstadt">University of Ingolstadt</a> in 1472, and the wedding of George to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hedwig-jagiellon-duchess-of-bavaria">Hedwig Jagiellon</a> in 1475 was among the most lavish festivals of the age.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>George died in 1503 without sons, leaving his lands to his son-in-law <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rupert-of-germany">Rupert of the Palatinate</a> in breach of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-wittelsbach">Wittelsbach</a> house law. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-landshut-succession">War of the Landshut Succession</a> of 1503 to 1505 gave most lands to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albert-iv-duke-of-bavaria">Albert IV of Bavaria-Munich</a>, while <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/palatinate-neuburg">Palatinate-Neuburg</a> was created for Rupert's sons.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/duchy-of-bavaria-landshut.jpg" alt="Duchy of Bavaria-Landshut" width="320" height="320"><figcaption>Image: Sir Iain · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Banner_of_Bavaria-Landshut.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1392 CE – 1503 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>duchy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Landshut</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Henry XVI the Rich, Louis IX the Rich, George the Rich</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Bavarian German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Bayern-Landshut</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1448&amp;focus=duchy-of-bavaria-landshut" aria-label="Duchy of Bavaria-Landshut on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4962 481 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Duchy of Bavaria-Landshut lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5282 737L5279 723M5282 737L5264 731M5282 737L5259 732"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5279 723h0M5264 731h0M5259 7